WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.325
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:14.595 --> 00:15.595
Yasa-chan.

3
00:17.315 --> 00:19.485
Whoa, you scared me!

4
00:19.615 --> 00:20.945
What is it?

5
00:21.155 --> 00:24.084
Call it a hunch, but...

6
00:24.085 --> 00:25.085
Yeah?

7
00:25.625 --> 00:28.255
You got a boyfriend recently, didn't you?

8
00:29.425 --> 00:32.195
Oh, stop it! No, I didn't.

9
00:33.465 --> 00:36.165
That reaction totally gives you away!

10
00:37.295 --> 00:38.305
Well, that's because...

11
00:39.065 --> 00:41.065
I didn't get a boyfriend.

12
00:41.375 --> 00:42.905
I got a girlfriend.

13
00:44.575 --> 00:46.575
A customer just asked me

14
00:46.705 --> 00:49.515
if we have any dry sake to recommend.

15
00:49.915 --> 00:52.985
Is that the new flame?

16
00:53.045 --> 00:54.226
The one in the back and the yellow bottle should both be dry.

17
00:54.250 --> 00:55.770
Not a chance in hell.

18
00:55.955 --> 00:57.485
Ah, this bottle right here.

19
00:57.925 --> 01:00.225
Got it, thanks.

20
01:06.265 --> 01:08.094
What about you, Miwa?

21
01:08.095 --> 01:10.265
Got your eye on anyone?

22
01:10.465 --> 01:11.465
Huh?

23
01:13.605 --> 01:14.605
Hey!

24
01:15.335 --> 01:17.875
They literally just broke up!

25
01:18.105 --> 01:19.305
I know, I just figured...

26
01:19.845 --> 01:23.645
I don't really have the right to, anyway.

27
02:03.205 --> 02:10.705
"How Do We Relationship?"

28
02:15.605 --> 02:18.304
(Episode 7: If There Was a Mistake)

29
02:18.305 --> 02:20.235
Can I post this on my story?

30
02:20.865 --> 02:21.975
I mean, sure,

31
02:22.335 --> 02:24.575
but people are gonna talk again.

32
02:24.745 --> 02:26.605
Asking if we got back together and stuff.

33
02:26.775 --> 02:30.015
Huh? We've been broken up for a month now.

34
02:30.545 --> 02:32.985
We're basically just strangers at this point.

35
02:41.655 --> 02:43.095
What about that girl from before?

36
02:43.155 --> 02:44.795
Isn't she your girlfriend?

37
02:47.765 --> 02:50.635
And what would you do if I said she was?

38
02:52.135 --> 02:53.365
Well, I...

39
02:55.795 --> 02:57.205
I wouldn't do anything.

40
02:59.745 --> 03:01.575
I guess I'd feel relieved for you.

41
03:02.145 --> 03:04.615
Because I want you to meet someone great

42
03:04.645 --> 03:07.285
and be really happy.

43
03:10.555 --> 03:13.385
- Mind your own business! - Ah!

44
03:14.855 --> 03:17.455
Besides, she's not my girlfriend anyway.

45
03:17.495 --> 03:19.594
I'm perfectly happy on my own!

46
03:19.595 --> 03:20.225
Hold on!

47
03:20.226 --> 03:22.265
How much of that are you gonna eat?!

48
03:25.935 --> 03:27.035
What about you, Miwa?

49
03:27.975 --> 03:29.834
What happened with your senpai from high school?

50
03:29.835 --> 03:31.345
Haven't you reached out to her?

51
03:34.045 --> 03:35.445
No, I haven't.

52
03:37.235 --> 03:43.508
Besides, how could I? She's basically the reason we broke up.

53
03:44.015 --> 03:45.225
Fair point.

54
03:45.855 --> 03:47.685
Normally, that would really piss me off.

55
03:51.895 --> 03:52.965
Right?

56
04:00.805 --> 04:01.905
Man...

57
04:04.335 --> 04:05.675
What's wrong?

58
04:06.745 --> 04:08.425
Why don't you just go get rejected by her?

59
04:09.915 --> 04:10.915
Huh?

60
04:11.145 --> 04:13.025
If you confess and get dumped, then we're good.

61
04:13.185 --> 04:14.185
Actually,

62
04:14.345 --> 04:15.345
Hmm...

63
04:16.015 --> 04:18.325
you should just go for it and tell her how you feel.

64
04:18.385 --> 04:20.345
You've been pining over her for years now, right?

65
04:21.295 --> 04:22.825
I couldn't possibly...

66
04:22.995 --> 04:24.394
That just wouldn't be fair to you.

67
04:24.395 --> 04:25.424
Why not?

68
04:25.425 --> 04:27.765
If you get dumped, I won't even be mad.

69
04:31.065 --> 04:32.065
Okay, but what if...

70
04:33.325 --> 04:34.404
we actually end up dating?

71
04:34.405 --> 04:35.705
What will you do then?

72
04:39.345 --> 04:41.215
- What's so funny? - Nothing, it's just...

73
04:41.275 --> 04:45.785
How can you say that with a straight face?

74
04:47.515 --> 04:48.515
Sorry...

75
04:49.715 --> 04:50.885
I wouldn't do anything.

76
04:52.285 --> 04:54.325
I'd just say congratulations.

77
05:08.555 --> 05:09.605
Miwa.

78
05:09.935 --> 05:13.045
You like someone, don't you?

79
05:13.345 --> 05:14.345
Huh?

80
05:15.545 --> 05:16.545
How did you know?

81
05:16.692 --> 05:21.021
Remember last time when you said you didn't have the right?

82
05:21.045 --> 05:24.415
That basically means there's someone on your mind.

83
05:27.185 --> 05:29.395
Ooh, silent treatment!

84
05:29.425 --> 05:32.525
You can be so sly sometimes, Miwa.

85
05:34.435 --> 05:36.035
Even though we broke up,

86
05:36.735 --> 05:38.905
I still feel guilty about it.

87
05:41.035 --> 05:43.374
I don't get that at all.

88
05:43.375 --> 05:45.745
I've never felt guilty a day in my life.

89
05:45.905 --> 05:50.845
Everyone would be way happier if they just did whatever they wanted.

90
05:54.555 --> 05:55.555
I get it now.

91
05:56.655 --> 05:58.155
Rika, you're...

92
05:58.585 --> 06:00.285
It's not that you're a free spirit.

93
06:00.855 --> 06:03.155
You're just extremely self-centered.

94
06:06.205 --> 06:09.795
You really don't pull any punches, Miwa.

95
06:09.935 --> 06:12.935
I could never live like that.

96
06:14.165 --> 06:15.935
Really?

97
06:16.475 --> 06:22.745
Because I think you're actually just as greedy as I am, Miwa.

98
06:24.135 --> 06:29.114
You don't want anyone to hate you, and you always want to be in the right.

99
06:29.115 --> 06:32.835
At the end of the day, you just want to protect this ideal image you have of yourself, right?

100
06:33.055 --> 06:35.825
It's all just to make yourself feel good.

101
06:38.425 --> 06:39.425
Well, I guess I'm just...

102
06:40.565 --> 06:42.865
greedy and selfish, then.

103
06:44.165 --> 06:46.904
Huh? What did you say?

104
06:46.905 --> 06:48.175
Wait, what? Say that again!

105
06:48.835 --> 06:49.835
Huh?

106
06:50.405 --> 06:51.475
I said,

107
06:51.965 --> 06:55.045
I'm just a greedy, selfish person!

108
07:00.515 --> 07:04.415
And that's what I love about you, Miwa.

109
07:09.555 --> 07:12.795
No, it's a girlfriend!

110
07:12.865 --> 07:15.995
Wait, a girlfriend? Seriously?!

111
07:16.765 --> 07:17.935
Not a boyfriend?

112
07:18.135 --> 07:19.435
Yep, that's right!

113
07:19.565 --> 07:21.005
Pretty wild, huh?

114
07:23.635 --> 07:25.745
I mean...

115
07:27.305 --> 07:29.145
I didn't know you were into girls too.

116
07:30.275 --> 07:31.845
Well...

117
07:31.915 --> 07:33.585
She told me,

118
07:33.785 --> 07:36.014
"It'd be such a waste

119
07:36.015 --> 07:40.655
to let only guys fall for a girl as amazing as you."

120
07:40.725 --> 07:42.094
That's what she said!

121
07:42.095 --> 07:44.255
Smooth talker.

122
07:44.625 --> 07:48.334
And I was like, "You know what? She has a point!"

123
07:48.335 --> 07:49.995
Wish I had your self-esteem!

124
07:51.565 --> 07:53.564
That's great, though.

125
07:53.565 --> 07:54.775
It's very you, Yuria.

126
08:00.345 --> 08:01.915
Happy for you, Yuria.

127
08:04.015 --> 08:05.515
Thank you!

128
08:06.045 --> 08:07.045
All right!

129
08:09.685 --> 08:10.685
All done!

130
08:11.455 --> 08:13.355
Your hair's all set.

131
08:15.025 --> 08:16.094
Wow!

132
08:16.095 --> 08:17.595
- Thank you. - Anytime!

133
08:26.025 --> 08:28.975
Since it's you, Yuria, I feel like I can actually say this.

134
08:29.435 --> 08:30.435
Huh?

135
08:34.415 --> 08:35.875
To tell you the truth...

136
08:36.615 --> 08:38.445
The person I was dating before

137
08:39.505 --> 08:41.455
was actually a girl, too.

138
08:42.355 --> 08:43.355
Wait...

139
08:43.955 --> 08:45.655
Wait, seriously?!

140
08:45.985 --> 08:48.354
That makes me so happy! We're in the same club!

141
08:48.355 --> 08:49.355
- The same club? - Uh-huh!

142
08:50.805 --> 08:51.805
Yeah, I guess we are.

143
08:57.485 --> 08:58.485
Inuzuka.

144
09:01.435 --> 09:02.875
Shiho senpai!

145
09:20.825 --> 09:22.325
I brought you a souvenir.

146
09:22.995 --> 09:25.925
Wow, thank you!

147
09:29.735 --> 09:31.615
Is there anywhere in particular you want to go?

148
09:31.935 --> 09:34.165
Um, well...

149
09:34.805 --> 09:36.335
I actually did...

150
09:36.675 --> 09:37.975
a little bit of...

151
09:38.245 --> 09:40.445
research on some places.

152
09:43.575 --> 09:45.545
You call this "a little bit"?!

153
09:46.415 --> 09:47.955
Let me see.

154
09:52.065 --> 09:53.895
This really takes me back.

155
09:54.285 --> 09:58.165
You used to highlight every single thing in your textbooks, too.

156
09:59.965 --> 10:02.965
You still remember that?

157
10:03.035 --> 10:04.035
Of course.

158
10:05.505 --> 10:08.505
I remember everything about you.

159
10:11.305 --> 10:12.605
You do?

160
10:14.715 --> 10:15.815
Today,

161
10:16.415 --> 10:18.535
let's do all the things we never got to do back then.

162
10:19.685 --> 10:20.685
Huh?

163
10:30.345 --> 10:31.595
The breeze feels amazing.

164
10:33.185 --> 10:34.995
- Is that good? - It's delicious.

165
10:35.925 --> 10:37.295
Let me have a sip.

166
10:37.635 --> 10:38.635
Huh?

167
10:40.305 --> 10:42.475
Mmm! That is good.

168
10:44.965 --> 10:47.915
Aw, how cute! It looks great on you!

169
11:01.325 --> 11:02.455
Sae-chan.

170
11:03.735 --> 11:05.324
Look at your face right now.

171
11:05.325 --> 11:09.364
It screams, "My ex is finally moving on to someone new."

172
11:09.365 --> 11:10.514
Does not!

173
11:10.515 --> 11:11.704
It totally does.

174
11:11.705 --> 11:12.734
Good work today!

175
11:12.735 --> 11:13.964
Hey, good work.

176
11:13.965 --> 11:16.465
Hey, Yasa-chan,

177
11:16.565 --> 11:18.875
how are things going with your girlfriend?

178
11:19.905 --> 11:21.075
Oh...

179
11:22.175 --> 11:23.515
We broke up.

180
11:23.775 --> 11:25.344
She was five-timing me.

181
11:25.345 --> 11:26.915
- Huh? - Five...

182
11:26.945 --> 11:28.131
Five-timing?! How is that even possible?!

183
11:28.155 --> 11:30.855
I know, it was insane!

184
11:31.145 --> 11:34.455
Apparently, she tried to schedule back-to-back dates with all of us,

185
11:34.705 --> 11:38.025
and we all ended up running into each other at once!

186
11:38.565 --> 11:40.724
And she just stood there grinning the whole time!

187
11:40.725 --> 11:42.595
What a total scumbag!

188
11:42.965 --> 11:44.464
Right?!

189
11:44.465 --> 11:48.295
Well, I bet that put you off girls for good, huh?

190
11:48.535 --> 11:51.304
Huh? Why would it?

191
11:51.305 --> 11:51.975
Wait...

192
11:51.976 --> 11:55.615
Because you weren't exclusively into girls to begin with, right?

193
11:55.945 --> 11:58.921
So having your first experience blow up like that, wouldn't it make you think...

194
11:58.945 --> 12:01.315
"Never doing that again"?

195
12:02.305 --> 12:04.085
Hmm...

196
12:04.925 --> 12:06.185
Well,

197
12:06.555 --> 12:08.725
even if a guy did that to me,

198
12:09.155 --> 12:12.795
I wouldn't swear off men for the rest of my life, you know?

199
12:14.165 --> 12:17.665
I don't think gender really has anything to do with it.

200
12:20.805 --> 12:23.935
That's what I love about you, Yuria.

201
12:27.245 --> 12:28.245
Huh?

202
12:30.975 --> 12:33.485
Do you really have to get that flustered?

203
12:34.325 --> 12:36.885
I'm not! Who's flustered?!

204
12:36.915 --> 12:38.255
You clearly are.

205
12:39.805 --> 12:40.905
Sorry, sorry.

206
12:44.105 --> 12:45.625
Back then, Inuzuka, you told me,

207
12:46.545 --> 12:50.535
"You have to take charge of your own happiness," remember?

208
12:51.805 --> 12:53.035
Hearing you say that

209
12:57.135 --> 13:01.775
finally made me want to start living my life for myself.

210
13:05.615 --> 13:07.385
Even if it took me a while to get there.

211
13:12.525 --> 13:13.525
So really,

212
13:16.055 --> 13:18.965
you're my savior, Inuzuka.

213
13:19.935 --> 13:22.695
You're someone very special to me.

214
13:25.465 --> 13:27.465
I just wanted to tell you that today.

215
13:30.235 --> 13:31.245
Thank you,

216
13:32.245 --> 13:33.245
Inuzuka.

217
13:37.175 --> 13:39.945
Your savior, huh?

218
13:52.325 --> 13:53.665
Shiho senpai.

219
13:55.145 --> 13:56.145
I...

220
13:59.335 --> 14:00.935
I don't want to just be your savior.

221
14:03.335 --> 14:04.645
Not your savior,

222
14:05.425 --> 14:06.905
and not just your underclassman.

223
14:09.845 --> 14:11.445
I want to be your girlfriend.

224
14:14.125 --> 14:15.214
I'm in love with you,

225
14:15.215 --> 14:16.485
Shiho senpai.

226
14:18.725 --> 14:20.385
Ever since high school,

227
14:21.555 --> 14:22.995
I've always been in love with you.

228
14:26.765 --> 14:27.995
Inuzuka...

229
14:40.575 --> 14:41.645
I'm sorry.

230
14:45.345 --> 14:47.485
I can't go out with you.

231
14:49.925 --> 14:51.584
It's not that I don't like you,

232
14:51.585 --> 14:53.555
and it's not because you're a girl.

233
14:59.405 --> 15:01.495
I dated someone a while back.

234
15:02.625 --> 15:04.705
He was a guy.

235
15:05.505 --> 15:07.465
He confessed to me, too,

236
15:09.005 --> 15:11.445
and I respected him as a person, so I said yes.

237
15:13.905 --> 15:16.315
I figured we could make it work somehow.

238
15:20.605 --> 15:21.605
Yeah...

239
15:23.145 --> 15:24.145
But in the end,

240
15:25.865 --> 15:26.865
I just couldn't do it.

241
15:29.695 --> 15:31.925
My heart wasn't fully in it,

242
15:33.125 --> 15:34.995
and I think he picked up on that.

243
15:38.935 --> 15:40.535
I ended up hurting him really badly.

244
15:43.775 --> 15:45.805
It was so irresponsible of me.

245
15:50.305 --> 15:51.305
And I...

246
15:52.045 --> 15:54.315
I don't want to make the same mistake again.

247
15:54.885 --> 15:58.685
Especially not with someone who means as much to me as you do.

248
16:02.645 --> 16:03.825
I wouldn't care...

249
16:05.165 --> 16:08.311
Even if we were only together for a fleeting moment, that would be enough for me.

250
16:08.335 --> 16:10.365
Could we not even have that?

251
16:14.405 --> 16:15.405
I'm sorry.

252
16:17.705 --> 16:18.705
Well then, let me...

253
16:20.275 --> 16:21.775
put it another way.

254
16:23.275 --> 16:25.615
I really didn't want to have to say this,

255
16:29.285 --> 16:31.765
but the courage it takes to face the world and its judgment...

256
16:33.105 --> 16:34.455
I just don't have it in me.

257
16:38.265 --> 16:39.265
But...

258
16:42.065 --> 16:44.095
there are people out there who understand!

259
16:44.565 --> 16:45.765
I know that.

260
16:46.535 --> 16:47.535
But still...

261
16:48.375 --> 16:50.475
Just knowing there are people who won't understand

262
16:52.105 --> 16:53.105
terrifies me.

263
16:56.245 --> 16:57.885
And it's not just the hostility.

264
17:00.285 --> 17:02.015
It's the overbearing concern,

265
17:03.225 --> 17:04.225
and the pity...

266
17:06.105 --> 17:08.755
I've had enough of all of it.

267
17:14.535 --> 17:16.395
I really do care about you, Inuzuka.

268
17:20.245 --> 17:21.245
But...

269
17:22.635 --> 17:23.635
I'm sorry.

270
17:29.945 --> 17:31.174
I'm truly sorry.

271
17:31.175 --> 17:32.375
Okay, I got it!

272
17:33.625 --> 17:35.155
I understand completely.

273
17:38.325 --> 17:41.125
I'm really glad I got to hear how you honestly feel.

274
17:45.085 --> 17:46.795
Thanks to you, I finally have closure.

275
17:47.665 --> 17:49.065
Thank you, senpai.

276
18:02.045 --> 18:04.615
Things must feel pretty awkward for you right now, huh?

277
18:05.785 --> 18:10.215
Honestly, it's pretty awkward for me too...

278
18:10.285 --> 18:11.825
And a little embarrassing.

279
18:12.665 --> 18:14.545
So let's just call it a day and part ways here.

280
18:15.525 --> 18:16.525
Are you sure?

281
18:19.325 --> 18:20.325
Well,

282
18:21.435 --> 18:23.235
I'll reach out to you again later.

283
18:24.805 --> 18:26.205
Get home safe.

284
18:27.635 --> 18:28.975
I'll get going now!

285
19:21.595 --> 19:22.625
Miwa?

286
19:22.825 --> 19:23.955
Are you okay?

287
19:24.465 --> 19:25.765
I came to check on you.

288
19:27.195 --> 19:28.195
You didn't have to.

289
19:29.035 --> 19:31.705
I'm fine. Just leave me alone.

290
19:31.715 --> 19:33.065
How is this "fine"?!

291
19:33.165 --> 19:35.035
You've skipped classes for a whole week!

292
19:35.275 --> 19:36.705
Are you feeling sick or something?

293
19:37.355 --> 19:39.275
I'm fine, just go home already.

294
19:39.305 --> 19:40.705
Wait, what?

295
19:47.355 --> 19:49.615
Keep it down, you're gonna bother the neighbors!

296
19:55.825 --> 19:57.425
Your room is a total pigsty!

297
19:58.495 --> 19:59.965
And it's pitch dark in here.

298
20:02.955 --> 20:04.365
I'm opening the window!

299
20:17.915 --> 20:19.945
Would you just get out of here already?

300
20:21.755 --> 20:23.315
What's with the attitude?!

301
20:24.355 --> 20:25.884
Anyway, have you seen a doctor?

302
20:25.885 --> 20:27.085
Did you take your temperature?

303
20:27.355 --> 20:28.825
I don't know.

304
20:29.725 --> 20:30.955
Who cares.

305
20:31.425 --> 20:32.425
Huh?

306
20:46.345 --> 20:48.375
Oh, right!

307
20:50.375 --> 20:54.615
I bought a bunch of groceries! I'll whip up a Saeko Special for you!

308
20:55.955 --> 20:58.085
I didn't ask for your help.

309
20:58.125 --> 20:59.425
What was that?

310
20:59.515 --> 21:01.195
Can't hear you!

311
21:11.865 --> 21:13.205
Serves me right...

312
21:19.415 --> 21:21.315
Here, just take one bite.

313
21:21.375 --> 21:22.445
Come on.

314
21:46.105 --> 21:47.765
Eat up and go back to sleep.

315
21:49.135 --> 21:50.935
I'll come by again tomorrow.

316
21:52.405 --> 21:53.905
Don't bother.

317
21:56.015 --> 21:57.985
Knew you'd say that.

318
21:58.985 --> 22:00.945
Look at you, you're a total mess right now.

319
22:02.055 --> 22:04.555
If I hadn't shown up, you probably would've starved to death!

320
22:07.555 --> 22:08.955
I don't care if I starve.

321
22:09.925 --> 22:11.155
I might as well just die.

322
22:12.265 --> 22:13.295
I wanna die.

323
22:13.725 --> 22:16.435
Oh, so that's how we're talking now?!

324
22:16.865 --> 22:18.565
Then I'm confiscating these noodles!

325
22:20.405 --> 22:22.535
People who wanna die don't need food anyway!

326
22:25.495 --> 22:26.495
Mmm, so good!

327
22:26.675 --> 22:28.245
Am I an udon genius or what?

328
22:29.875 --> 22:33.915
As long as you stay alive, I'll make this for you whenever you want!

329
22:36.555 --> 22:37.555
Stop it.

330
22:40.475 --> 22:42.325
You're only making me feel more pathetic.

331
22:42.755 --> 22:44.315
Honestly, you're being really annoying.

332
22:45.565 --> 22:48.095
Huh? What do you mean, "annoying"?!

333
22:48.695 --> 22:50.495
You're the annoying one here!

334
22:51.155 --> 22:52.795
What the hell are you moping around for?!

335
22:53.335 --> 22:55.095
Stop acting so fragile just to get sympathy!

336
22:55.805 --> 22:58.374
Shut up and go home already!

337
22:58.375 --> 22:59.405
Huh?

338
23:00.235 --> 23:02.415
Do you really hate me that much?!

339
23:19.465 --> 23:20.465
What are you doing?

340
23:21.665 --> 23:23.165
Let go of me.

341
23:31.805 --> 23:35.245
Please don't leave me...

342
23:36.775 --> 23:38.415
Don't leave me all alone...

343
23:43.905 --> 23:46.405
(Final Episode Preview)

344
23:47.735 --> 23:48.894
Let's do it one more time.

345
23:48.895 --> 23:50.324
We make pretty good friends with benefits, right?

346
23:50.325 --> 23:51.695
We're the worst.

347
23:51.725 --> 23:53.564
Even though you can't even bear to look at me.

348
23:53.565 --> 23:55.135
I've wanted to die this whole time.

349
23:55.165 --> 23:58.435
There's no way we can go back to being friends now.

350
24:01.759 --> 24:03.759
MkvDrama.net
